markdown <<MARKDOWN
# Understanding AI

#### Understanding how AI generates text can help prevent falling into the pitfalls in the previous levels. The most important thing to understand about AI is its relationship to reality. AI models do not perceive the world—they generate text solely based on patterns learned from language.

#### Because of this, AI can produce fluent, convincing text, but it depends entirely on humans to supply grounding, verify accuracy, and interpret results. Misunderstandings often occur when users expect AI to “know” facts or reason logically, when in reality it is only producing statistically likely sequences of words.

<div style="text-align: center; width: 80%; margin: 0 auto;">
  <p style="
    font-size: 18px; 
    background-color: #F5F7F8; 
    padding: 10px; 
    border-left: 5px solid #8148B2; 
    border-right: 5px solid #8148B2;
    display: inline-block;
  ">
    AI predicts and generates language patterns extremely well, but humans must provide context, verify outputs, and make final decisions.
  </p>
</div>

---

## How AI Works

#### The following sections explain some of the underlying mechanisms behind how AI works so you can use AI more effectively and responsibly.


>#### **💬 Quick Reflection:** As you're reviewing the text below, think about what questions do you still have about how AI works. Make note of them now - on the next level you'll have a chance to ask AI Chat Lab questions, get clarification, or dive deeper into any specific concepts.

<details style="background-color: #ececec; padding: 10px; margin-bottom: 10px; border: 1px solid transparent; border-radius: 5px;">
    <summary style="font-size: 1.5em;"><strong>Training: Learning Patterns in Language, Not Facts</strong></summary>

<div style="margin-top: 20px; margin-left: 20px; margin-right: 20px; padding-bottom:20px;">

<div style="display:flex;gap:16px;align-items:flex-start;">
<img src="https://images.code.org/4302af15f049172a62d1df03d6cc8b1d-Screenshot 2026-01-29 at 1.19.23 PM.png" alt="" style="width: 100px; border-radius:8px; flex-shrink:0;">
<div>
<p>

#### AI models are trained on massive text datasets—books, articles, websites, and conversations. Training does not teach facts, rules, or understanding. Instead, the model learns statistical patterns by predicting missing or next words in sequences. When a prediction is wrong, the model adjusts its internal parameters to improve future predictions.
#### Crucially, this training does not provide real-world knowledge. The model cannot perceive events or update itself after training. Once complete, its knowledge is frozen; it can only reproduce patterns it saw in its training data, not current or future reality.

</p></div>
</div>
</div>
</details>

<details style="background-color: #ececec; padding: 10px; margin-bottom: 10px; border: 1px solid transparent; border-radius: 5px;">
    <summary style="font-size: 1.5em;"><strong>Embeddings: Capturing Relationships in Language</strong></summary>

<div style="margin-top: 20px; margin-left: 20px; margin-right: 20px; padding-bottom:20px;">

<div style="display:flex;gap:16px;align-items:flex-start;">
<img src="https://images.code.org/4302af15f049172a62d1df03d6cc8b1d-Screenshot 2026-01-29 at 1.19.23 PM.png" alt="" style="width: 100px; border-radius:8px; flex-shrink:0;">
<div>
<p>

#### During training, the model creates embeddings, numerical representations of words and concepts. Words and ideas that frequently appear together, like “teacher,” “student,” and “classroom,” are positioned close together in a high-dimensional space, while unrelated concepts are distant.
#### Embeddings allow the model to detect patterns of similarity and analogy in text, but they do not convey understanding. The AI does not know what a classroom is—it only knows how words relate statistically. This is why AI can switch between related ideas fluidly, yet still miss important situational or human-relevant context.

</p></div>
</div>
</div>
</details>

<details style="background-color: #ececec; padding: 10px; margin-bottom: 10px; border: 1px solid transparent; border-radius: 5px;">
    <summary style="font-size: 1.5em;"><strong>Next-Token Prediction: Generating Text Step by Step</strong></summary>

<div style="margin-top: 20px; margin-left: 20px; margin-right: 20px; padding-bottom:20px;">

<div style="display:flex;gap:16px;align-items:flex-start;">
<img src="https://images.code.org/4302af15f049172a62d1df03d6cc8b1d-Screenshot 2026-01-29 at 1.19.23 PM.png" alt="" style="width: 100px; border-radius:8px; flex-shrink:0;">
<div>
<p>

#### Once prompted, the model generates language one token at a time, predicting the most probable next word based on the text so far. Attention mechanisms determine which parts of the input should influence each prediction, helping the model maintain coherence across long passages and follow instructions.
#### However, attention is purely statistical. It does not verify facts, reason about correctness, or assess appropriateness. The model can produce confident explanations, logical step-by-step outputs, or even persuasive arguments without knowing if they are accurate or meaningful.

</p></div>
</div>
</div>
</details>

<details style="background-color: #ececec; padding: 10px; margin-bottom: 10px; border: 1px solid transparent; border-radius: 5px;">
    <summary style="font-size: 1.5em;"><strong>Steering Output: Temperature and System Prompts</strong></summary>

<div style="margin-top: 20px; margin-left: 20px; margin-right: 20px; padding-bottom:20px;">

<div style="display:flex;gap:16px;align-items:flex-start;">
<img src="https://images.code.org/4302af15f049172a62d1df03d6cc8b1d-Screenshot 2026-01-29 at 1.19.23 PM.png" alt="" style="width: 100px; border-radius:8px; flex-shrink:0;">
<div>
<p>

#### Finally, humans can shape the model’s outputs using temperature settings and system prompts. Temperature controls randomness: low temperatures produce predictable, conservative outputs, while high temperatures allow creativity and variation. System prompts can set tone, role, or style—for instance, instructing the model to “act as a middle school science teacher.”
#### These tools influence presentation and style, but not understanding or judgment. A confident, playful, or authoritative tone is a reflection of statistical probabilities, not comprehension. The AI still operates solely on patterns learned from text.

</p></div>
</div>
</div>
</details>


<br>

<div style="font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, Segoe UI, Roboto, Arial, sans-serif; max-width: 1100px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 20px; position: relative;">
